  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CHT - St&#xe4;rkt demokratisk samh&#xe4;llsstyrning &amp; MR</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHT Conflict Prevention, Recovery &amp; Peacebuilding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Government institutions at the national and subnational levels are able to more effectively carry out their mandates, including devlivery of public services, in a more accountable, transparent and inclusive manner.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sverige &#xe4;mnar st&#xf6;dja  det av UNDP implementerade projektet &quot;Conflict Prevention, Recovery and Peace-Building in Chittagong Hill Tracts of Bangladesh&quot; med totalt SEK 3,500,000 under 2014 och 2015. Projektet syftar till att st&#xf6;dja implementeringen av det fredsavtal fr&#xe5;n 1997 som innebar slutet p&#xe5; en 25 &#xe5;r l&#xe5;ng v&#xe4;pnad konflikt i CHT. Projektet ska bidra till det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let p&#xe5; tre s&#xe4;tt: 1) genom att st&#xf6;dja f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad policy dialog och p&#xe5;verkansarbete f&#xf6;r implementering av fredsavtalets alla delar; 2) genom att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten hos institutioner p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5; att arbeta med f&#xf6;rtroendeskapande och social sammanh&#xe5;llning; och 3) genom att bygga upp en mekanism f&#xf6;r st&#xf6;d till offer f&#xf6;r etniskt v&#xe5;ld.  

Projektet st&#xf6;djs, vid sidan av Sverige, av UNDPs Bureau for Crisis Prevention and Recovery samt Danmark, och &#xe4;r en del i det st&#xf6;rre UNDP-st&#xf6;dda programmet, Chittagong Hill Tracts Development Facility.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sweden intends to support the UNDP-implemented project &quot;Conflict Prevention, Recovery and Peace-Building in the Chittagong Hill Tracts of Bangladesh&quot; with a total of SEK 3,500,000 in 2014 and 2015. The project aims to support the implementation of the CHT Peace Accord from 1997 which ended a 25-year long armed conflict in the CHT. The project will contribute to the overall goal in three ways: 1) by supporting improved policy dialogue and advocacy for the full implementation of the Peace Accord; 2) by strengthening the capacity of institutions at the local level to work on confidence building and social cohesion; and 3) by building a mechanism to assist the victims of communal violence. 

The project is supported, in addition to Sweden, by the UNDP Bureau for Crisis Prevention and Recovery, and Denmark, and is a part of the larger UNDP-supported programme Chittagong Hill Tracts Development Facility.</narrative>
  </description>
